# Jott Translator - Phase 1 (Tokenizer)

## Group Members (GROUP 1)
Authors: Conner Meagher, Anindita Bhowmik, Borniel Gope, Jatin Jain


## Project Structure
- `provided/`: Top-level package containing the base compiler lifecycle files (`JottTokenizer.java`, `Token.java`, `TokenType.enum`, etc.).
- `testers/`: Contains the test runner classes (`JottTokenizerTester.java`, `JottParserTester.java`).
- `tokenizerTestCases/`: Working directory folder containing the raw `.jott` testing files.

## Building and running the code

From the repo root:

```bash
mkdir -p bin
javac -d bin project_files/provided/*.java project_files/testers/*.java
```

Running the Tokenizer Tester
Because the test runners depend on relative directory paths to locate test cases, navigate into the directory containing the test data before executing:

```bash
cd project_files
java -cp ../bin testers.JottTokenizerTester
```

## PHASE 2 

Once you setup and have compiled the files above; you should be able to run the following cmds from the repo root and vlidate the tests 

```bash
cd project_files
java -cp ../bin testers.JottParserTester
```
